# Merriam-Webster API keys — TEMPLATE. This file is tracked; .env is not.
#
# Copy it and fill in the copy:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Then run the ingest with:
#
#   node --env-file-if-exists=.env tools/fetch-words.js --limit=20
#
# NEVER put a real key in this file. It is committed. Real keys go in .env,
# which is gitignored — and .env is the only file you need to carry between
# machines. Nothing else in the repo knows a key exists.
#
# Keys are free, and this project ships none: register at
# https://dictionaryapi.com/register/index
#
# M-W issues ONE KEY PER REFERENCE WORK, so two dictionaries means two
# registrations and two keys. Request the Elementary dictionary first — it is
# the one written for this age group, and it is the only one that is required.

# Elementary Dictionary (sd2). Required. Grades 3-5 — the primary source.
MW_KEY=

# Intermediate Dictionary (sd3). Optional. Grades 6-8, used only as a fallback
# for words Elementary does not carry. Leave it empty if you did not register a
# second key; the ingest simply skips that pass. Having it doubles the daily
# budget, since the 1000-queries-per-day cap is PER REFERENCE, not per account.
MW_KEY_INTERMEDIATE=
